## Spatial and temporal transition map

| Window | Front | Living middle | Rear / residue | Required transition owner |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0–5 min | Cardamom capsule, beta-pinene, dry pepper, aldehydic rind | Linalyl/linalool seam and first Bontoux lavender | First cedar grain and coumarin shadow | Linalyl Acetate + Terpinyl Acetate prevent citrus/cardamom separation |
| 5–30 min | Cold pod shell narrows | Three lavenders, regular Hedione near-space, Hedione HC rear-space | Coumarin/Tonkarome and first fatty seed tissue | Dihydrojasmone + Jessemal turn aromatic shell into warm interior |
| 30–120 min | Aromatic residue and bitter-green incision | Natural tonka, heliotropal, damascenone, immortelle, dry bark | AIMI/ionone/Irotyl cloth and Suederal pressure | Damascenone + Beta Ionone + Dihydro Beta Ionone turn seed into complexion |
| 2–6 h | Violet-green fiber | Cedar/vetiver verticals and differentiated sandalwood chamber | Buried rails and mineral contour | Orivone + Vetikon + Vetival connect root cloth to wood grain |
| 6 h+ | Dry aromatic memory | Coumarinic wood, soft suede pressure, and creamy skin | Transparent amberwood line and long dry contour | Linalyl, ionone, coumarin, wood, and EB relationships recall cardamom without pretending the top remains unchanged |

All temporal language is design intent, not observed evolution.

